<title>UK: Whitbread says completes hotel sale.</title>
<headline>Whitbread says completes hotel sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brewer to leisure group Whitbread Plc said on Friday it has completed the sale of 13 three star hotels to the Regal Hotel Group for 64.5 million stg.</p>
<p>The sale was first announced in April and forms part of Whitbread's plan to focus on its four star and budget hotels through the Marriott and Travel Inn chains.</p>
<p>Last year the group's hotel business contributed about 50 million stg to profits and is the third largest hotel group in Britain with almost 13,500 rooms.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
